    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0538" n="468" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg468"/>

                <head>Mr. Plumb to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 27.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">City of Mexico,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-10-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 31, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of a note addressed to me by M. Farine, in charge of French interests here,
                    received yesterday, in which he officially asks my confirmation of the document
                    referred to in my despatch No. 18, of the 18th instant, a copy of which he also
                    encloses with his note.</p>
                <p>I have replied to M. Farine that having to await new instructions upon the
                    general subject involved, I am unable to act in the premises at present. A copy
                    of my reply is also transmitted herewith.</p>
                <p>I have desired to manifest every courtesy to M. Farine, not only because be
                    appears to be a very discreet person, every way worthy of confidence, but from
                    motives of deference to the country whose interests are in his charge.</p>
                <p>Trusting my action in this matter will meet with your approval, I am, very
                    respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E.L. PLUMB.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Sewabd,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



